[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:24. It Could Be Worse]
[00:00.640]Passage 24 | 文章二十四
[00:02.620]It could be worse. | 事情可能会更糟。
[00:05.455]I entered the hotel manager's office | 我走进酒店经理的办公室
[00:09.310]and sat down. | 然后坐了下来。
[00:11.215]I had just lost 50 pounds | 我刚刚丢了50英镑
[00:14.445]and I felt very upset. | 我感到非常沮丧。
[00:17.015]I left the money in my room, | 我把钱落在我的房间里了，
[00:20.270]I said, | 我说，
[00:21.260]and it's not there now. | 而且它现在不在那里了。
[00:23.995]The manager was sympathetic, | 经理表示同情，
[00:26.690]but he could do nothing. | 但他无能为力。
[00:29.110]Everyone's losing money these days, | “现在每个人都在亏钱，
[00:32.425]he said. | 他说。
[00:33.855]He started to complain about this wicked world, | 他开始抱怨这个邪恶的世界，
[00:37.640]but was interrupted by a knock at the door. | 但被敲门声打断了。
[00:40.730]A girl came in | 一个女孩走了进来
[00:42.795]and put an envelope on his desk. | 把一个信封放在他的桌子上。
[00:45.425]It contained 50 pounds. | 里面有50英镑。
[00:48.615]I found this outside this gentleman's room, | “我是在这位先生的房间外面找到这个的，”
[00:51.810]she said. | 她说。
[00:53.475]Well, | “嗯，
[00:55.315]I said to the manager, | 我对经理说，
[00:57.055]there is still some honesty | 这个世界上
[00:59.660]in this world. | 仍然存在一些诚实。